Teach node.gyp to hand clang-cl to the ninja generator (our own change, not upstream)

Why this patch exists: since Node 24 the Windows build is supposed to use clang-cl
(BUILDING.md: "As of Node.js 24.0.0, ClangCL is required to compile on Windows"), but
`./configure --clang-cl=<version>` only records the toolchain in the generated config -
it does not change which compiler ninja runs. gyp's ninja generator looks up cl.exe
through the Visual Studio environment and keeps using it, while the flags Node puts on
the command line are chosen by the `clang=1` variable the same option sets. The result
is a build that asks for clang-style settings and compiles with MSVC, and loses the C++
standard completely (see docs/node-26.md).

gyp has one supported way to pick another compiler on Windows: a `make_global_settings`
entry whose CC path ends in "clang-cl" (see
tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/generator/ninja.py: "If we have selected clang-cl, use that
instead."). Node has no make_global_settings anywhere, so this patch adds one, driven
by a `clang_cl` variable that stays empty unless the caller passes -Dclang_cl=<path>.
Node's ./configure forwards its leftover arguments to gyp, so the CI job passes
-Dclang_cl=/path/to/clang-cl. The condition keeps every other platform untouched.

Verified on Linux by generating ninja files with the Windows flavour:

    cl_x64 = /path/to/clang-cl -m64
    cl_x86 = /path/to/clang-cl -m32

--- a/node.gyp
+++ b/node.gyp
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 {
   'variables': {
+    'clang_cl%': '',
     'v8_use_siphash%': 0,
     'v8_trace_maps%': 0,
     'v8_enable_pointer_compression%': 0,
@@ -1768,6 +1769,16 @@
   ], # end targets
 
   'conditions': [
+    # gyp's ninja generator finds cl.exe through the Visual Studio environment and
+    # has no other knob for choosing a different compiler. It does honour one thing:
+    # a make_global_settings CC whose path ends with "clang-cl" makes it use that
+    # compiler for every architecture (adding -m64/-m32). Node's ./configure passes
+    # its leftover arguments on to gyp, so -Dclang_cl=<path to clang-cl> gets here.
+    ['OS=="win" and clang_cl!=""', {
+      'make_global_settings': [
+        ['CC', '<(clang_cl)'],
+      ],
+    }],
     ['OS=="win" and node_shared=="true"', {
      'targets': [
        {
